# Not formatted yet: the frontend and backend source. Debt, and it shrinks to nothing.
#
# codebase-mcp's tools read these two trees with regexes that only see a declaration written on
# one line, and prettier writes long ones over several. Measured 2026-11-22 by calling every tool
# before and after a format of all of code/: form-validation-rules lost two whole schemas
# (customDistroSchema, vmCreateSchema), storage-adapters lost every method whose signature now
# spans lines, store-signatures split one multi-line action into four bogus ones, and
# api-endpoints lost a route's role, because it looks for requireRole in a fixed 500-character
# window. form-validation-rules and store-signatures live in codebase-mcp-base, shared
# byte-for-byte with the template, so their parsers are fixed there and synced. When all four
# read a formatted tree the same as this one, delete these two lines and run `npm run format`.
/src/
/backend/src/
# A byte-for-byte copy of src/constants/vocabularies.ts (audit:vocabulary), so it is formatted
# when its canonical is, and goes with the two lines above.
/tui/src/constants/vocabularies.ts

# Not formatted yet: four files where a rewrap would force text to change. audit:decision-refs
# counts an id on an added line as newly written, excusing only a line whose text also left the
# same hunk, and a rewrapped line has new text. In three of them the ids are test data, so a
# title would go inside the very strings under test (a code comment naming an id, a
# decision-table row) and change what they test. In compliance-frameworks.ts the id sits in
# capability prose that gen:compliance-matrix renders into customer-facing sales docs, so a title
# would publish internal release planning as a side effect of a format. The checker is shared
# with the template. When its predicate reads a rewrap as unchanged, delete these and run
# `npm run format`.
/scripts/data/compliance-frameworks.ts
/scripts/verify-published-comments.ts
/testing/unit/scripts/historical-context.spec.ts
/testing/unit/scripts/verify-superseded-architecture.spec.ts
